            <ArticleTitle>[Value of manometry].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>955-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Manometry of the esophagus is essential in the diagnostic workup of patients with motility disorders of the esophagus. Before manometry organic diseases causing the symptoms should be excluded by a esophago-gastroscopy and/or a barium swallow meal. Indications for manometry are noncardiac chest pain, dysphagia of unknown origin, primary or secondary motility disorders of the esophagus and preoperative assessment before antireflux surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
